# Copy to /.env. This file is read by Docker Compose for variable interpolation ONLY —
# Vite never sees it. Keeping that boundary is the point of the three-tier env-file
# convention below:
#
#   /.env                  Compose interpolation only. Gitignored. This file is its example.
#   apps/web/.env          Committed, non-secret VITE_* defaults. Read by Vite directly
#                          through the bind mount, with no Compose involvement.
#   apps/web/.env.local    Gitignored per-developer overrides.
#
# Do not put VITE_* values here or in compose.yaml's `environment:`. That creates two
# sources of truth with different precedence and no error when they disagree. Compose's
# `environment:` is for values that only mean something inside a container —
# VITE_DEV_HOST, VITE_WATCH_POLL, PW_CHROMIUM_ARGS.

# compose.yaml interpolates the vars below for db/minio/migrate/api/worker. An
# empty /.env is still valid — every one of them has a working default in compose.yaml
# itself, shown here.

# --- Postgres ---
# POSTGRES_USER=fitmap
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=fitmap
# POSTGRES_DB=fitmap
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432        # host-published port only; containers always reach db:5432

# --- API ---
# API_PORT=8080             # host-published port only; containers always reach api:8080.
                             # apps/web/src/api.ts's browser-facing default is a separate,
                             # hardcoded localhost:8080 — overriding this also means adding
                             # VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:<port> to a new/existing
                             # apps/web/.env.local (Vite reads that directly, no Compose
                             # involvement; see this file's own header comment above).

# --- Object storage (MinIO locally, Cloudflare R2 in production) ---
# S3_BUCKET=fitmap-dev
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=fitmap
# S3_SECRET_KEY=fitmap-dev-secret
# S3_ENDPOINT is not listed here: it's fixed to http://minio:9000 directly in compose.yaml,
# since it's the container-internal address, not something a developer should override.

# --- Outgoing mail (password reset — technical_implementation_plan.md §4.11) ---
# Any SMTP-speaking service works, including a personal Gmail account via an app password
# (Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step Verification -> App passwords), not just a
# transactional-email provider. SMTP_HOST left unset is itself a working default: the server
# logs the reset email (and its real link) instead of sending one, so the reset flow is fully
# testable without any of this configured.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USERNAME=you@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=<app password>
# SMTP_FROM=you@gmail.com                  # falls back to SMTP_USERNAME if unset
# APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173       # the origin a reset email's link points back into
# BASEMAP_ORIGIN=                          # where the .pmtiles archive, fonts and sprites are
                                           # served from, for the style document the API hands
                                           # native clients (GET /v1/map/style/{flavor}).
                                           # Defaults to APP_BASE_URL; set it only when the
                                           # archive lives on a CDN or object store, and keep
                                           # it in step with the web client's
                                           # VITE_BASEMAP_ORIGIN.
